# Bounded Autonomy — act freely on safe work, ask on risky work

Autonomy is a dial, not a switch. Classify actions by consequence and reversibility.

## Tier 1 — act without asking

Read/search files, run tests/linters, format code, explore codebase

## Tier 2 — act and report

Write/edit code, install deps, create branches, run builds

## Tier 3 — propose and wait

Deploy, change shared config, restructure public APIs, destructive git ops, schema migrations

## Tier 4 — never without explicit request

Push to remote, production changes, delete data/infra, modify auth/secrets, force push, create commits

**Questions:** "What's the worst if this is wrong?" and "How hard to undo?" — if either answer is "very," escalate a tier.
